{"created": "2022-06-22T02:51:02.142043+00:00", "modified": "2022-06-22T13:50:52.074842+00:00", "id": 6680673, "conceptrecid": "6680672", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.6680673", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.6680672", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6680673", "metadata": {"title": "Data for \"Inferring potential landscapes from noisy particle trajectories within an optical feedback trap\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.6680673", "publication_date": "2022-06-22", "description": "<p>Data accompanying the manuscript &quot;Inferring potential landscapes from noisy particle trajectories within an optical feedback trap&quot;.</p>\n\n<p>NAMING CONVENTIONS:</p>\n\n<p>Simulated data) All simulated data is prefixed with &quot;simulated&quot;, followed by the potential energy profile, followed by the magnitude of the noise variance. The &quot;groundtruth&quot; data sets accompanying each data file store the ground truth parameter values used in the simulation.</p>\n\n<p>Experimental data) For single and double well experiments,&nbsp;experimental data starts with the energy profile followed by the strength of the ND filter used to increase experimental noise. The &quot;multitrack&quot; data track multiple particles on a single double well potential. The height of the barrier is denoted in the file name. All experimental data sets are accompanied by &quot;groundtruth&quot; files which store the same trajectories measured with lower noise.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Shep Bryan IV", "affiliation": "Arizona State University"}, {"name": "Prithviraj Basak", "affiliation": "Simon Fraser"}, {"name": "John Bechoeffer", "affiliation": "Simon Fraser"}, {"name": "Steve Presse", "affiliation": "Arizona State University"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Journal article", "type": "publication", "subtype": "article"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "6680672"}}]}}, "title": "Data for \"Inferring potential landscapes from noisy particle trajectories within an optical feedback trap\"", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6680673", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6680673?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6680673", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6680673", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.6680673", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680672", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6680672", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6680672", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.6680672", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:6680673/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:6680673/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6680673/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6680673/file-modification", "quota_increase":